<title>MONACO: MOTOR RACING-MICHAEL SCHUMACHER WINS MONACO GRAND PRIX.</title>
<headline>MOTOR RACING-MICHAEL SCHUMACHER WINS MONACO GRAND PRIX.</headline>
<dateline>MONTE CARLO 1997-05-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Michael Schumacher of Germany, driving a Ferrari, won Sunday's Monaco Grand Prix motor race.  </p>
<p>Brazilian Rubens Barrichello finished second in a Stewart,</p>
<p>with Britain's Eddie Irvine third in a Ferrarri.</p>
<p>Olivier Panis of France was fourth in a Prost, with Finland's</p>
<p>Mika Salo fifth in a Tyrrell and Italy's Giancarlo Fisichella</p>
<p>sixth in a Jordan.</p>
<p>World drivers' championship standings (after five rounds):</p>
<p> 1. Michael Schumacher (Germany)	    24 points</p>
<p> 2. Jacques Villeneuve (Canada)	     20</p>
<p> 3. Eddie Irvine (Britain)		    14</p>
<p>4 equal. Heinz-Harald Frentzen (Germany) 10</p>
<p> 4 equal.David Coulthard (Britain)	  10</p>
<p> 4 equal.Gerhard Berger  (Germany)	  10</p>
<p> 4 equal. Mika Hakkinen (Finland)	   10</p>
<p> 8. Olivier Panis (France)		     9</p>
<p> 9. Rubens Barrichello (Brazil)		6</p>
<p> 10 equal.Ralf Schumacher (Germany)	  4</p>
<p> 10 equal. Giancarlo Fisichella (Italy)    4</p>
<p> 12.equal Johnny Herbert (Britain)	   3</p>
<p> 12 equal. Jean Alessi (France)		3</p>
<p> 14. Mika Salo (Finland)			 2</p>
<p> 15. Nicola Larini (Italy)		     1</p>
<p>Constructors' championship:</p>
<p> 1. Ferrari					 38 points</p>
<p> 2. Williams					30</p>
<p> 3. McLaren-Mercedes			    20</p>
<p> 4. Benetton-Renault			    13</p>
<p> 5. Prost					    9</p>
<p> 6. Jordan					   8</p>
<p> 7. Stewart					  6</p>
<p> 8. Sauber-Petronas				4</p>
<p> 9. Tyrrell					  2</p>
</text>
